WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.445 --> 00:00:02.960
- [Narrator] In Seoul, South Korea,

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.096
there's a woman who is
mixing a century's old

00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:09.179
Korean instrument with
the music of rock legends.

00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:12.025
Her name is Luna Lee.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.759
The gayageum dates back to 400 B.C.,

00:00:41.759 --> 00:00:43.636
and was often played during celebrations

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:45.303
at the Royal Palace.

00:00:54.428 --> 00:00:57.261
(energetic music)

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:05.229
(applause)

00:01:06.268 --> 00:01:08.832
To modernize her
gayageum, Luna added amps,

00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:11.508
used thinner strings
and adjusted the height

00:01:11.508 --> 00:01:14.591
to create a slightly different sound.

00:01:38.599 --> 00:01:41.098
Her videos have hundreds
of thousands of views.

00:01:41.098 --> 00:01:43.681
This one has over four million.

00:01:45.308 --> 00:01:49.111
- Hello guys, I'm gonna play one song.

00:01:49.111 --> 00:01:51.531
Hope you like it (laughs).

00:01:51.531 --> 00:01:52.364
Thank you!

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:07.716
(soft music)

